<title>USA: Osborn gets early end of antitrust period.</title>
<headline>Osborn gets early end of antitrust period.</headline>
<dateline>GREENWICH, Conn. 1996-12-05</dateline>
<text>
<p>Osborn Communications Corp said it received early termination of the antitrust waiting period for its proposed merger with Capstar Broadcasting Partners Inc.</p>
<p>Capstar was formed by the investment firm Hicks, Muse, Tate &amp; Furst Inc and radio industry executive R. Steven Hicks.</p>
<p>Capstar agreed in July to buy Osborn for $15.375 a share or more than $100 million in cash. The deal is expected to close at the end of February.</p>
<p>Separately, Osborn said the U.S. Federal Communications Commission approved the transfer of control of Osborn to Capstar. Final approval of the transfer is expected in mid-January.</p>
<p>-- New York Newsdesk 212-859-1610</p>
